"'''Jack & Diane'''" is a song written and performed by American singer-songwriter [[John Mellencamp]], then performing as "John Cougar". Described by critics as a "love [[Sentimental ballad|ballad]]",<ref>{{cite web|last=Lee|first=Peter|date=May 9, 2008|title=Play Guitar Like John Cougar Mellencamp|url=https://hooksandharmony.com/you-too-can-play-guitar-like-john-cougar-mellencamp/|access-date=February 12, 2021|website=Hooks and Harmony}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last=Miller|first=Hanna|date=July 6, 2005|title=Hurts so good|url=https://mountainx.com/arts/art-news/0706jackdiane-php/|access-date=February 12, 2021|website=[[Mountain Xpress]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last=Zhe|first=Mike|date=August 31, 2012|title=No looking back for champion Clipper football team|url=https://www.seacoastonline.com/article/20120831/NEWS/208310399|access-date=February 12, 2021|website=[[The Portsmouth Herald|seacoastonline.com]]}}</ref> this song was released as the second single from Mellencamp's 1982 album ''[[American Fool]]'', and was chosen by the [[Recording Industry Association of America]] (RIAA) as one of the [[Songs of the Century]]. It spent four weeks at [[Chart-topper|number one]] on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] in October <ref>Billboard Hot 100 October 2-23 1982</ref> 1982 and is Mellencamp's most successful hit single.

